## 2. Component Diagram

### Description
A Component Diagram shows the **physical / logical building blocks** of the system and
how they communicate through interfaces. It answers: *"What are the deployable pieces and
what does each one depend on?"*

The Multimedia Analyzer is broken into five layers:

| Layer | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Entry Point** | `main.py` — CLI interface, argument parsing, pipeline coordinator |
| **Utility** | `file_utils.py` — extension-based type detection |
| **Analyzers** | `image_analyzer.py`, `audio_analyzer.py`, `video_analyzer.py` — extract metadata |
| **Processors** | `img_enhance.py`, `voice_cloning.py` — transform/enrich media |
| **Output** | `report_generator.py` — persist results as JSON |

External dependencies:
- **Pillow** — image open, EXIF read, enhancement filters (`ImageAnalyzer`, `ImageEnhancer`)
- **FFprobe (subprocess)** — audio/video metadata (`AudioAnalyzer`, `VideoAnalyzer`)
- **ElevenLabs Scribe API** — cloud speech-to-text (`VoiceCloning`)
- **File System** — reads input files, writes `reports/*.json` and `enhanced_image.jpg`

